// Live rooms: a WebSocket room whose sockets receive the room's state as
// per-viewer snapshots instead of raw events.
//
//   trigger event (core NATS, queue group: one replica)
//     → build the room state from the database (the endpoint's state op)
//     → publish it to JetStream  live.<endpoint>.<room>  with a compare-and-set
//       on the subject's last sequence, so stream order = build order
//   every replica (ordered consumer on live.<endpoint>.>)
//     → keeps the latest state of each room in memory
//     → derives the view once per viewer company (the endpoint's view op, no
//       database) and sends a socket a frame only when its view changed
//   reconnect with ?since=<seq>
//     → the states after <seq> are replayed from the stream (or, when they
//       are gone or too many, the latest one with reset=true)
//
// Frames: {"type":"RoomSnapshot","payload":{"seq","at","reset","view"}} and
// {"type":"RoomSync","payload":{"seq","at"}} (seq 0 = no stored state yet).
// A viewer the view op denies is closed with 4403.
//
// Environment: LIVE_ROOMS=off disables it; LIVE_ROOMS_MAX_AGE (24h),
// LIVE_ROOMS_MAX_PER_ROOM (200), LIVE_ROOMS_REPLAY_MAX (50),
// LIVE_ROOMS_STORAGE (file|memory), LIVE_ROOMS_REPLICAS (1).

